GNU gantt NEWS -- history of user-visible changes.

* Noteworthy changes in release 2.0.0 (2026-09-25)

** Versioning

  Releases now use Semantic Versioning (MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH), hence 2.0.0.

** Build system

  gantt now uses the GNU build system: ./configure && make && make install.
  The compiled helper programs (gantt_copy, gantt_delete, ...) and the helper
  scripts (gantt_zip, gantt_tar, ...) are now installed into the same
  directory as gantt itself, so no extra PATH setup is needed.  'make check'
  runs the test suite.

** Licence

  gantt is now distributed under the GNU GPL version 3 or later (previously
  stated as version 2 or later).

** New features

  New SAX-style direct parser for improved performance.
  New tasks: <parallel>, <sequential>, <condition>, <native2ascii>, <apply>,
  <pathconvert>, <xmlproperty>, and the ivy tasks (including ivy:publish).
  New <javaversion> condition, nested <manifest> in <jar>, <selector>
  elements in <javac>, incremental compilation in <javac>, OS/platform
  filtering for <exec>, and input redirection for <exec> and <java>.
  Property capture (outputproperty, errorproperty, resultproperty).
  Native C implementations of copy, delete, move, touch, chmod, mkdir and
  concat.
  Profiling support via the GANTT_PROFILE environment variable.

** Bug fixes

  <echo> now honours file= and append= (it is a built-in task).
  Nested <manifest> in <jar> and nested tasks in <parallel> and <sequential>
  were being ignored, and are now handled.  New tasks <untar>, <gzip>,
  <gunzip>, <bzip2> and <bunzip2>.

** Changes

  XML parsing uses expat instead of libxml2.

See CHANGELOG.md for the full list, and ChangeLog for the commit history.

* Noteworthy changes in release 1.0 (2005-02-18)

  Initial release.

